WEBVTT

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:10.090
Pessimist:

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:13.590
One who is distressed about the world,
despondent about one's life,

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:15.970
and single-mindedly
discouraged about the future.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:20.640
That describes people like me to a T.

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:26.060
Though born into a family of means,

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:29.570
I grew up without a single
drop of love from my family.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.440
The coup de grâce?

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:38.160
I was in an accident--and lost everything.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:39.870
My mother,

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:41.620
the use of my right hand,

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:43.410
and

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.750
my father's expectations.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:48.920
You <i>would </i>have to ruin your dominant hand.

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:51.710
A good-for-nothing has
no place in the Shima family.

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:53.670
Get out of my sight.

00:00:56.470 --> 00:01:00.310
I was sent off to our villa
in the mountains of Chiba.

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:06.480
As though I were a
nuisance just being alive,

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:08.610
and I should die, alone.

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:13.110
Yes: this is my final dwelling.

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:30.590
♬ In the moonless sky I see them ♬

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:34.800
♬ Tiny lights that twinkle so ♬

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:42.180
♬ There, in those starry shadows ♬

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:49.350
♬ See the shape of hope aglow ♬

00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:56.820
My life has ended after 17 years.

00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:02.530
I see nothing--no light to
illuminate my way forward.

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:05.500
There's nothing... nothing.

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:10.790
How much easier it would be
if I simply never woke up...

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.210
Begging your pardon!

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:18.380
Good evening!

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:27.890
Who could it be, deep in these
mountains on a snowy night?

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:34.230
And you are?

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:38.740
A pleasure to meet you, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>.

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:42.780
My name is Yuzuki.

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:47.200
I've come here to be your bride,
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:08.810
"Taisho Otome Fairy Tale"

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:19.090
"Taisho Otome Fairy Tale"

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:24.050
"Episode 1"
"Yuzuki Arrives"

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:34.060
Come to think of it, my father
did mention something that day...

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:40.320
There's no one in the Shima family
able to care for you now.

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:41.900
I suppose I have no choice.

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:45.820
I'll buy you a bride or
something to look after you.

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:49.490
That's my father.

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:53.000
Most likely this girl was
being sold to cover a debt.

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:00.340
Don't want to catch a cold.

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:08.760
But why send a bride
to a dead man walking?

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:09.760
Um...

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:14.770
You may use this room as you wish.

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:18.900
It's entirely pointless.

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:31.200
Another day begins
without a wink of sleep.

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:39.380
Wh-What are you doing?!

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:42.420
Oh! Good morning, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>!

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:44.420
And what a lovely morning it is!

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:47.430
Look: last night's snow
has already begun to melt.

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:54.310
Will you wash your face?

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:56.940
I'll help!

00:05:56.940 --> 00:05:58.400
I can do it myself.

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:01.730
I want to be helpful!
Please let me take care of you.

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:05.190
Well, yes, but...

00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:10.950
Y-You don't have to dry me off!

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:12.660
Oh, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>!

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:18.710
Such dark circles.
Are you having trouble sleeping at night?

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:19.710
Not...

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:24.000
Not particularly.
And it's no concern of yours.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.550
Please, let me be.

00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:30.050
I've made breakfast...

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:31.340
I'm not hungry.

00:06:33.510 --> 00:06:35.520
And every day'll be like this?

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:38.180
Pardon me!

00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:39.560
I'll just do some cleaning.

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:55.830
I've been shopping in town!

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:57.000
You certainly are strong...

00:06:59.830 --> 00:07:01.920
A nice big serving! Eat up!

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:02.920
Impossible.

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:05.630
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>!

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:09.840
There was a hole,
but I patched it for you!

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:12.640
My long johns!

00:07:13.640 --> 00:07:15.680
You just go around
mending men's underwear?

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:20.310
Underwear?!

00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:22.560
It's a little late to be so scandalized.

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:28.400
I've been all out of sorts
ever since that girl showed up.

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:32.490
Here I thought I'd slowly
rot away in obscurity.

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:34.990
How irritating.

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:39.000
Don't even have time...
to get lost... in thought.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:40.750
I'm coming in!

00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:41.870
What?!

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:43.460
I'll rinse your back!

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:47.500
Pl-Please don't trouble yourself!

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:48.710
Oh, I will.

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:50.670
It must be hard to do one-handed.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:58.140
What gives?

00:07:58.140 --> 00:08:00.600
What <i>is </i>this girl thinking?

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:05.060
Given her speech and mannerisms,

00:08:05.060 --> 00:08:08.020
she was likely a pampered-princess type.

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:10.320
An innocent girl who
knows little of the world.

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:16.620
I bet you haven't a
single worry to speak of.

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:18.490
--Why, that's awful!
--Eh?

00:08:18.490 --> 00:08:20.370
I certainly <i>do </i>have a worry.

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:21.790
Two of them, in fact!

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:26.630
Is that all?

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:31.460
But to me, both of them are big worries.

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:37.180
That's right--she was sold
to pay off a debt.

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:39.600
The unspeakable agony
of coming into the world...

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:42.810
One of them...

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:45.850
"floof"

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:52.240
...is my hair--I have so much,
and it's so wavy!

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:53.240
Huh?

00:08:54.070 --> 00:08:56.740
I know--it's weird!
And it's way too fluffy!

00:08:56.740 --> 00:09:00.040
I'd love to have shiny,
straight hair, but nothing works!

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:02.410
All I can do is braid it!

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:05.120
That's... your worry?

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:09.710
I can't believe I showed you!

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:21.390
Sorry.

00:09:21.390 --> 00:09:24.270
So <i>that's </i>what you look
like when you laugh.

00:09:24.270 --> 00:09:25.270
Huh?

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:28.770
If it made you smile, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>...

00:09:28.770 --> 00:09:31.980
I think I'm starting to
warm up to this hair.

00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:38.240
Enough. Leave me in peace!

00:09:41.990 --> 00:09:43.910
She's on my last nerve.

00:09:54.550 --> 00:09:57.050
This <i>monaka </i>sweet is delicious!

00:09:57.050 --> 00:09:58.590
Try these, too.

00:09:58.590 --> 00:10:01.010
And these--they're tasty!

00:10:01.010 --> 00:10:06.310
Are you sure? I'm always
eating everyone else's treats...

00:10:06.310 --> 00:10:08.060
It's perfectly fine.

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:10.310
After all, Yuzuki,
when you're on meal duty,

00:10:10.310 --> 00:10:12.900
we always eat more than usual!

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:17.400
It's a sin to make a maiden
eat even one bite more!

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:21.660
Th-Then I'll just have
to atone for my sins!

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:22.910
Very good.

00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:26.000
Yuzuki! I fell!

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:28.870
And see this here? It's all torn!

00:10:28.870 --> 00:10:30.380
All right.

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:31.540
Let's sew that right up.

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:36.090
"poke pull"

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:42.640
She's such a mom.

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:44.010
She really is.

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:47.100
Thanks, Yuzuki!

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:50.480
You really will make a
wonderful bride someday!

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:51.480
A bride...

00:10:54.020 --> 00:10:58.950
Actually, there's something
I need to tell you all...

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:04.030
I... I'm leaving the girls' school.

00:11:05.450 --> 00:11:08.000
But why? This is all so sudden!

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:10.710
It's embarrassing to talk about...

00:11:10.710 --> 00:11:13.630
but my parents are deep in debt,

00:11:13.630 --> 00:11:17.840
so I'm to be married
to their lender's son.

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:18.920
No!

00:11:19.880 --> 00:11:25.180
B-But women can't marry until they're 15!

00:11:25.180 --> 00:11:26.770
Right.

00:11:26.770 --> 00:11:32.310
But certain circumstances mean
I'll be leaving to take care of him.

00:11:32.310 --> 00:11:34.560
Yuzuki...

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:38.490
No matter what he's like,
no matter what his circumstances,

00:11:38.490 --> 00:11:41.150
I'll just do my best and
be with him for always.

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:46.910
After all, he's my dearest husband.

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:51.960
It's all right.

00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:57.250
I know you can do it,
no matter who you'll be marrying.

00:11:57.250 --> 00:12:00.720
I mean, you work twice
as hard as anyone else!

00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:02.930
Midori...

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:08.680
You must... you must...

00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:10.480
...be happy!

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:11.480
I will!

00:12:23.030 --> 00:12:27.740
"December 31, Taisho 10 (1921)"

00:12:31.710 --> 00:12:34.000
The New Year's Eve bell...

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:36.750
So it's the dawn of another year.

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:42.010
A new year, and my life
is the same as ever.

00:12:50.720 --> 00:12:51.980
I can't sleep.

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:15.170
All these thoughts
running through my head...

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:18.290
Get out of my sight.

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:21.590
Your dominant hand?
You've failed as the second Shima son.

00:13:21.590 --> 00:13:26.130
Aren't <i>you </i>fancy,
retiring at such an early age.

00:13:26.130 --> 00:13:28.850
<i>You </i>should have died instead of Mother!

00:13:30.470 --> 00:13:34.270
I couldn't care less if you went away.

00:13:34.270 --> 00:13:38.270
Farewell, useless good-for-nothing
brother of mine.

00:14:10.100 --> 00:14:13.520
May I stay up with you?

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:17.230
What's she thinking?

00:14:17.230 --> 00:14:19.190
As you like.

00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:20.400
Hooray!

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:22.110
Oh--I know!

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:27.530
The girl's a bother, too.

00:14:27.530 --> 00:14:31.120
If she were just a maid, I'd give
her the day off and send her out.

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:38.750
Don't you hate it?

00:14:38.750 --> 00:14:40.380
What's that?

00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:42.670
Being chased deep into the mountains here

00:14:42.670 --> 00:14:45.210
and given as a bride to a man like me.

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:48.880
Of course you do.

00:14:48.880 --> 00:14:51.260
Of <i>course </i>you'd hate it.

00:14:51.260 --> 00:14:54.680
A pessimist recluse
like me with no future--

00:14:54.680 --> 00:14:57.270
it must be torture simply
to live under the same roof!

00:14:57.270 --> 00:14:59.390
You must be cursing your own misfortune!

00:14:59.390 --> 00:15:02.860
Come now, don't hold back--
tell me how you <i>really </i>feel!

00:15:11.110 --> 00:15:14.580
Here. It's ready.

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:16.410
What is it?

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:17.750
It's delicious.

00:15:25.340 --> 00:15:28.470
It's sweet... and warm.

00:15:28.470 --> 00:15:31.680
I warmed up some milk and added sugar.

00:15:38.180 --> 00:15:40.730
Back in the dorms at the girls' school,

00:15:40.730 --> 00:15:43.940
we'd often stay up late drinking this.

00:15:44.940 --> 00:15:45.900
School?

00:15:47.690 --> 00:15:51.740
We'd chat about silly things,
sing songs...

00:15:53.530 --> 00:15:59.790
♬ In the moonless sky I see them ♬

00:15:59.790 --> 00:16:05.500
♬ Tiny lights that twinkle so ♬

00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:09.340
--♬ There, in those starry shadows ♬

00:16:09.340 --> 00:16:11.090
--This song...
--♬ There, in those starry shadows ♬

00:16:11.090 --> 00:16:14.470
--♬ See the shape of hope aglow ♬

00:16:14.470 --> 00:16:16.970
--My mother often sang that
to my little sister, long ago.
--♬ See the shape of hope aglow ♬

00:16:16.970 --> 00:16:18.470
--My mother often sang that
to my little sister, long ago.
--♬ Since our knowledge knows no limits ♬

00:16:18.470 --> 00:16:22.890
--♬ Since our knowledge knows no limits ♬

00:16:22.890 --> 00:16:27.690
♬ On some far-off day to come ♬

00:16:29.940 --> 00:16:31.950
What fun we had...

00:16:34.860 --> 00:16:38.450
I no longer think of going back to school.

00:16:38.450 --> 00:16:41.250
Think of all the hardships I'd encounter

00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:43.540
with this right hand of mine.

00:16:43.540 --> 00:16:47.090
I'm just... I'm fed up.

00:16:47.090 --> 00:16:49.670
Fed up with being unneeded...

00:16:49.670 --> 00:16:52.050
Fed up with being hurt...

00:16:53.590 --> 00:16:56.470
With every nightfall, I think:

00:16:56.470 --> 00:16:59.010
"I don't want to wake up."

00:16:59.010 --> 00:17:02.980
No one would even mourn my death.

00:17:04.640 --> 00:17:06.100
But...

00:17:06.100 --> 00:17:08.940
...the more I think about it,
the less I can sleep.

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:35.380
Why are you so kind to me?

00:17:36.840 --> 00:17:40.760
Not even my own family...
not one of them...

00:17:43.730 --> 00:17:47.270
When your father bought me
for 10,000 yen...

00:17:48.860 --> 00:17:53.860
...I said I wasn't afraid to be
the wife of a man I'd never met.

00:17:53.860 --> 00:17:55.240
That was a lie.

00:17:56.820 --> 00:18:00.490
But the first time I met you...

00:18:00.490 --> 00:18:02.120
Your coat goes there.

00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:03.700
R-Right.

00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:06.000
You must have walked a long way.

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:08.920
A-About 30 <i>chō</i>... or so.

00:18:13.090 --> 00:18:14.710
Don't want to catch a cold.

00:18:16.050 --> 00:18:19.140
He's so kind, and has such integrity.

00:18:20.100 --> 00:18:24.020
I'm sure he'll cherish me.

00:18:25.350 --> 00:18:31.940
So, I thought, I'll cherish <i>him</i>,
too, and be kind to him.

00:18:31.940 --> 00:18:34.230
Wha--Wh-Wh--

00:18:34.230 --> 00:18:36.530
What's your rationale for that?!

00:18:36.530 --> 00:18:38.860
Do you <i>always </i>take people at their word?

00:18:38.860 --> 00:18:41.870
Oh, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>!
Might we sleep together?

00:18:41.870 --> 00:18:43.240
Huh?!

00:18:43.240 --> 00:18:46.830
Just for tonight--
it's our first New Year holiday.

00:18:46.830 --> 00:18:50.250
Let's greet the first morning
of the new year together!

00:18:50.250 --> 00:18:52.040
Greet the morning--together?

00:18:55.710 --> 00:19:01.640
"thump-thump"

00:18:55.710 --> 00:19:01.640
What--how--what--how is this happening?!

00:19:01.640 --> 00:19:03.180
"huff huff"

00:19:01.640 --> 00:19:03.180
Wh-Wh-What do I do?

00:19:03.180 --> 00:19:08.180
I-it's my first time--
what am I supposed to d-d-d-do?

00:19:08.180 --> 00:19:10.440
I haven't the foggiest idea!

00:19:10.440 --> 00:19:12.440
Ah! That's right!

00:19:12.440 --> 00:19:14.480
I-It's around here somewhere...

00:19:14.900 --> 00:19:16.860
"Juicy Night-Time Club - Special Edition"
"Make Eros Yours"

00:19:18.950 --> 00:19:21.320
T-Terrifying!

00:19:21.320 --> 00:19:23.410
Pardon me!

00:19:23.410 --> 00:19:26.660
Huh? Separate futons?

00:19:26.660 --> 00:19:28.250
Good night!

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:35.550
"Sleep together"... "sleep together"...

00:19:35.550 --> 00:19:37.670
She really <i>did </i>mean "sleep... <i>together</i>"!

00:19:40.930 --> 00:19:43.550
I-I knew that.

00:19:48.680 --> 00:19:51.140
Would you have preferred
we share one futon?

00:19:52.020 --> 00:19:56.730
We mustn't! I'm still a virgin who's
never even been in love yet!

00:19:56.730 --> 00:19:59.780
That will have to wait
until we're married.

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:03.820
But...

00:20:03.820 --> 00:20:08.240
I <i>will </i>save myself for you, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>.

00:20:08.240 --> 00:20:09.700
You...

00:20:09.700 --> 00:20:11.370
Please, call me Yuzu.

00:20:14.170 --> 00:20:19.590
You would give your chastity
to a man you don't even love?

00:20:19.590 --> 00:20:20.800
I...

00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:27.220
I want to be at your side to see
all the different Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>s.

00:20:27.220 --> 00:20:28.600
I want to love you.

00:20:29.350 --> 00:20:30.980
That's what I think.

00:20:33.230 --> 00:20:34.770
Good night.

00:20:38.780 --> 00:20:40.070
What on earth...?

00:20:54.370 --> 00:20:57.090
I... I can't sleep.

00:20:57.090 --> 00:20:59.670
Another entirely sleepless night.

00:21:01.510 --> 00:21:02.880
Good morning!

00:21:05.930 --> 00:21:08.180
Good morning, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>.

00:21:11.020 --> 00:21:13.390
Happy New Year!

00:21:13.390 --> 00:21:15.350
I've made breakfast.

00:21:17.690 --> 00:21:19.650
I hope it's to your liking...

00:21:22.530 --> 00:21:24.570
What's this?

00:21:24.570 --> 00:21:29.030
<i>Hittsumi </i>dumpling soup. I thought you'd
get tired of New Year's dishes.

00:21:38.840 --> 00:21:40.170
Is it good?

00:21:41.550 --> 00:21:44.840
She really is one annoying girl.

00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:47.140
Oh, she wants to love me, does she?

00:21:49.180 --> 00:21:51.260
Can... can I get seconds?

00:21:51.260 --> 00:21:52.270
Sure!

00:21:53.220 --> 00:21:57.020
I'm a pessimist who hates
all this world has to offer!

00:21:57.020 --> 00:21:58.860
It's highly, <i>highly </i>unlikely.

00:22:01.940 --> 00:22:05.030
Me, love Yuzu?

00:23:38.540 --> 00:23:41.420
I want to take care of Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>

00:23:41.420 --> 00:23:44.840
wholeheartedly and with kindness.

00:23:44.840 --> 00:23:50.130
If I do, I'm sure Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>
will open his heart, too.
